{"name":"Evil Centipede","hex":"#aa2211","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"evil","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Intending to harm; malevolent.","Morally corrupt."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Moral badness; wickedness; malevolence; the forces or behaviors that are the opposite or enemy of good.","Something which impairs the happiness of a being or deprives a being of any good; something which causes suffering of any kind to sentient beings; harm; injury; mischief."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evil"},{"term":"centipede","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any arthropod of class Chilopoda, which have a segmented body with one pair of legs per segment and from about 20 to 300 legs in total.","A many-oared Chinese smuggling boat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/centipede"}],"entries":[{"title":"Evil","blocks":[{"text":"Evil, as a concept, is usually defined as profound immorality, and it is related to acts that cause pain and suffering to others."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Demon._A_miniature_from_the_Georgian_manuscript_of_the_12th_century.jpg/330px-Demon._A_miniature_from_the_Georgian_manuscript_of_the_12th_century.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evil"},{"title":"Centipede","blocks":[{"text":"Centipedes are predatory arthropods belonging to the class Chilopoda of the subphylum Myriapoda, an arthropod group which includes millipedes and other multi-legged animals. Centipedes are elongated segmented (metameric) animals with one pair of legs per body segment. All centipedes are venomous and can inflict painful stings, injecting their venom through pincer-like appendages known as forcipules or toxicognaths, which are actually modified front legs instead of fangs. Despite the name, no species of centipede has exactly 100 legs; the number of pairs of legs is an odd number that ranges from 15 pairs to 191 pairs. Less common names include \"forty-legs\" and \"hundred-legs\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Chilopoda_collage.png/330px-Chilopoda_collage.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centipede"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Ary_Scheffer_-_The_Temptation_of_Christ_%281854%29.jpg/500px-Ary_Scheffer_-_The_Temptation_of_Christ_%281854%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Ary_Scheffer_-_The_Temptation_of_Christ_%281854%29.jpg/1280px-Ary_Scheffer_-_The_Temptation_of_Christ_%281854%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Ary_Scheffer_-_The_Temptation_of_Christ_%281854%29.jpg/500px-Ary_Scheffer_-_The_Temptation_of_Christ_%281854%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The devil, in opposition to the will of God, represents evil and tempts Christ, the personification of the character and will of God. Ary Scheffer, 1854.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAry_Scheffer_-_The_Temptation_of_Christ_(1854).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Extermination_of_Evil_Sendan_Kendatsuba_crop.jpg/500px-Extermination_of_Evil_Sendan_Kendatsuba_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Extermination_of_Evil_Sendan_Kendatsuba_crop.jpg/1280px-Extermination_of_Evil_Sendan_Kendatsuba_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Extermination_of_Evil_Sendan_Kendatsuba_crop.jpg/500px-Extermination_of_Ev